# 必考词 Unit07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit07核心词汇

{{narrative}}{{/ˈnærətɪv}}{{n./adj. 叙述；叙事的；故事}}{{The novel has a compelling narrative.}}
{{nasty}}{{/ˈnɑːsti}}{{adj. 令人不快的；恶劣的；恶意的}}{{The weather turned nasty in the afternoon.}}
{{navigate}}{{/ˈnævɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 导航；航行；驾驶}}{{The captain navigated the ship through the storm.}}
{{negative}}{{/ˈneɡətɪv}}{{adj./n. 否定的；消极的；底片}}{{Try not to have a negative attitude towards life.}}
{{neglect}}{{/nɪˈɡlekt}}{{v./n. 忽视；疏忽；忽略}}{{He neglected his health and became ill.}}
{{negotiate}}{{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt}}{{v. 谈判；协商；商定}}{{The two sides negotiated a peace agreement.}}
{{nerve}}{{/nɜːv}}{{n. 神经；勇气；胆量}}{{It takes nerve to speak in front of a large audience.}}
{{network}}{{/ˈnetwɜːk}}{{n. 网络；网状系统；人际关系网}}{{The internet is a global computer network.}}
{{neutral}}{{/ˈnjuːtrəl}}{{adj. 中立的；中性的；不带色彩的}}{{Switzerland remained neutral during the war.}}
{{nevertheless}}{{/ˌnevəðəˈles}}{{adv. 然而；不过；尽管如此}}{{The task was difficult; nevertheless, they completed it.}}
{{niche}}{{/niːʃ}}{{n. 壁龛；合适的位置；利基市场}}{{She found her niche in the tech industry.}}
{{noble}}{{/ˈnəʊbl}}{{adj. 高尚的；贵族的；宏伟的}}{{He comes from a noble family.}}
{{nominate}}{{/ˈnɒmɪneɪt}}{{v. 提名；任命；推荐}}{{She was nominated for the best actress award.}}
{{nonetheless}}{{/ˌnʌnðəˈles}}{{adv. 尽管如此；然而；不过}}{{The evidence is weak; nonetheless, it cannot be ignored.}}
{{norm}}{{/nɔːm}}{{n. 标准；规范；准则}}{{Working from home has become the new norm.}}
{{notable}}{{/ˈnəʊtəbl}}{{adj. 值得注意的；显著的；著名的}}{{There has been a notable improvement in air quality.}}
{{notion}}{{/ˈnəʊʃn}}{{n. 概念；想法；意图；见解}}{{The notion of equality is central to democracy.}}
{{notorious}}{{/nəʊˈtɔːriəs}}{{adj. 声名狼藉的；臭名昭著的}}{{The area is notorious for its high crime rate.}}
{{notwithstanding}}{{/ˌnɒtwɪθˈstændɪŋ}}{{prep./adv. 尽管；虽然}}{{Notwithstanding the rain, the event was a success.}}
{{novel}}{{/ˈnɒvl}}{{n./adj. 小说；新颖的；新奇的}}{{She wrote her first novel at the age of 20.}}
{{nuclear}}{{/ˈnjuːkliər}}{{adj. 核的；核能的；原子核的}}{{Nuclear energy is a controversial topic.}}
{{nullify}}{{/ˈnʌlɪfaɪ}}{{v. 使无效；废除；取消}}{{The court nullified the contract.}}
{{numerous}}{{/ˈnjuːmərəs}}{{adj. 许多的；大量的；为数众多的}}{{Numerous studies have shown the benefits of exercise.}}
{{nurture}}{{/ˈnɜːtʃər}}{{v./n. 养育；培养；培育}}{{Parents nurture their children with love and care.}}
{{nutrition}}{{/njuˈtrɪʃn}}{{n. 营养；营养学；营养物}}{{Good nutrition is essential for children's growth.}}
{{obey}}{{/əˈbeɪ}}{{v. 服从；遵守；听从}}{{Citizens should obey the law.}}
{{object}}{{/ˈɒbdʒɪkt/{{n./v. 物体；目标；反对}}{{Many people objected to the new regulation.}}
{{objective}}{{/əbˈdʒektɪv}}{{n./adj. 目标；客观的；公正的}}{{The main objective of the project is to reduce costs.}}
{{obligation}}{{/ˌɒblɪˈɡeɪʃn}}{{n. 义务；责任；合约}}{{Paying taxes is an obligation of every citizen.}}
{{oblige}}{{/əˈblaɪdʒ}}{{v. 迫使；帮忙；感激}}{{I would be obliged if you could help me.}}
{{observe}}{{/əbˈzɜːv}}{{v. 观察；遵守；评论；庆祝}}{{Scientists observed the behavior of the animals.}}
{{obsolete}}{{/ˈɒbsəliːt}}{{adj. 过时的；废弃的；淘汰的}}{{The old technology has become obsolete.}}
{{obtain}}{{/əbˈteɪn}}{{v. 获得；得到；流行}}{{She obtained a degree in computer science.}}
{{obvious}}{{/ˈɒbviəs}}{{adj. 明显的；显而易见的；平淡的}}{{The answer is obvious to everyone.}}
{{occasion}}{{/əˈkeɪʒn}}{{n. 场合；时机；理由；起因}}{{This is a special occasion for the whole family.}}
{{occupy}}{{/ˈɒkjupaɪ}}{{v. 占据；使忙碌；居住于}}{{The meeting occupied the entire morning.}}
{{occur}}{{/əˈkɜːr}}{{v. 发生；出现；被想起}}{{The accident occurred at midnight.}}
{{offend}}{{/əˈfend}}{{v. 冒犯；违反；使不快}}{{I'm sorry if my words offended you.}}
{{offset}}{{/ˈɒfset}}{{v./n. 抵消；补偿；偏移}}{{The gains offset the losses.}}
{{offspring}}{{/ˈɒfsprɪŋ}}{{n. 后代；子女；产物}}{{The animal protects its offspring from predators.}}
{{ongoing}}{{/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ}}{{adj. 持续的；进行中的；不断发展的}}{{The ongoing negotiations are making progress.}}
{{operate}}{{/ˈɒpəreɪt}}{{v. 操作；经营；动手术；运转}}{{The doctor operated on the patient successfully.}}
{{opponent}}{{/əˈpəʊnənt}}{{n. 对手；反对者；敌手}}{{He defeated his opponent in the final match.}}
{{opportunity}}{{/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti}}{{n. 机会；时机；就业机会}}{{This is a great opportunity for young graduates.}}
{{oppose}}{{/əˈpəʊz}}{{v. 反对；对抗；与…竞争}}{{Many citizens opposed the construction of the factory.}}
{{oppress}}{{/əˈpres}}{{v. 压迫；压抑；使烦恼}}{{The people were oppressed by the dictator.}}
{{optimistic}}{{/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk}}{{adj. 乐观的；乐天的}}{{She is optimistic about the future of the company.}}
{{option}}{{/ˈɒpʃn}}{{n. 选项；选择权；买卖权}}{{You have three options to choose from.}}
{{orient}}{{/ˈɔːriənt}}{{v./n. 使适应；确定方向；东方}}{{The program helps new students orient themselves to college life.}}
{{origin}}{{/ˈɒrɪdʒɪn}}{{n. 起源；出身；原点}}{{The origin of the tradition dates back centuries.}}
{{original}}{{/əˈrɪdʒənl}}{{adj./n. 原始的；独创的；原件}}{{The original painting is in the museum.}}
{{otherwise}}{{/ˈʌðəwaɪz}}{{adv./adj. 否则；另外；不同地}}{{Hurry up; otherwise, we'll be late.}}
{{outcome}}{{/ˈaʊtkʌm}}{{n. 结果；后果；成果}}{{The outcome of the election surprised everyone.}}
{{outlet}}{{/ˈaʊtlet}}{{n. 出口；销路；插座；发泄途径}}{{The mall has many retail outlets.}}
{{outline}}{{/ˈaʊtlaɪn}}{{n./v. 轮廓；概述；提纲}}{{She outlined the main points of the plan.}}
{{output}}{{/ˈaʊtpʊt}}{{n. 产量；输出；产出}}{{The factory's output has doubled this year.}}
{{outrage}}{{/ˈaʊtreɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 愤怒；暴行；凌辱；引起愤怒}}{{The decision caused public outrage.}}
{{outstanding}}{{/aʊtˈstændɪng}}{{adj. 杰出的；未解决的；显著的}}{{She is an outstanding scientist in her field.}}
{{overcome}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈkʌm}}{{v. 克服；战胜；解决}}{{She overcame many difficulties to achieve her goal.}}
{{overlap}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈlæp}}{{v./n. 重叠；重复；交叉}}{{The two projects overlap in several areas.}}
{{overlook}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈlʊk}}{{v. 忽视；俯瞰；宽容}}{{Don't overlook the small details.}}
{{overseas}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈsiːz}}{{adv./adj. 海外的；在海外；国外的}}{{Many students choose to study overseas.}}
{{overtake}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈteɪk}}{{v. 超过；赶上；突然降临}}{{China has overtaken Japan in GDP.}}
{{overwhelm}}{{/ˌəʊvəˈwelm}}{{v. 压倒；使不知所措；淹没}}{{She was overwhelmed by the amount of work.}}
